ce  is a Thai-inspired dish which was created in Hawaiʻi in 1977 by Laotian American Keo Sananikone for his Mekong restaurant in Honolulu.  Later versions by Sananikone included other proteins.  Sananikone also created the evil princess, but that is a cocktail and not a related dish."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-evil-jungle-prince"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Evil_jungle_prince"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Hawaiian cuisine","cuisine/cuisine-of-hawaii"],["Thai cuisine","cuisine/thai-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":5,"links":[["Basil","ingredient/basil"],["Chicken","ingredient/chicken"],["Chili pepper","ingredient/chili-pepper"],["Coconut milk","ingredient/coconut-milk"],["Tofu","ingredient/tofu"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Onolicious Hawaii","ref":"site/onolicioushawaii-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"onolicioushawaii.com","note":"Hawaii-based blog of local-style recipes.","url":"https://onolicioushawaii.com","suggested":true},{"name":"Hot Thai Kitchen","ref":"site/hot-thai-kitchen-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"hot-thai-kitchen.com","note":"Pailin Chongchitnant's recipes and videos, with background on technique and ingredients.","url":"https://hot-thai-kitchen.com","suggested":true},{"name":"SheSimmers","ref":"site/shesimmers-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"shesimmers.com","note":"Bangkok-born writer Leela Punyaratabandhu's blog on Thai home cooking.","url":"https://shesimmers.com/who-is-shesimmers","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from Hawaiian cuisine","links":[["Ate-Oh-Ate","dish/ate-oh-ate"],["Butter mochi","dish/butter-mochi"],["Hula's Island Grill","dish/hula-s-island-grill"],["Poi (Hawaiian food)","dish/poi-hawaiian-food"]]}]},"dish/irving-street-kitchen":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/irving-street-kitchen","n":"Irving Street Kitchen","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from American cuisine","dot":"#94bd5c","intro":[["Irving Street Kitchen was a restaurant serving American cuisine in Portland, Oregon's Pearl District, in the United States. Conceived by Doug Washington, Mitch Rosenthal and Steve Rosenthal as their interpretation on American cuisine with a Southern influence, it opened on May 6, 2010. With executive chef Sarah Schafer, Irving Street Kitchen added to their serving hours over the years, opening up for lunch and brunch. The restaurant also shifted towards casual dining in 2019, revamping its menu and ambiance. Irving Street Kitchen ultimately closed during the COVID-19 pandemic."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-irving-street-kitchen"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Irving_Street_Kitchen"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["American cuisine","cuisine/american-cuisine"]]},{"h":"More from American cuisine","links":[["5-8 Club","dish/5-8-club"],["Altabira City Tavern","dish/altabira-city-tavern"],["Angel food cake","dish/angel-food-cake"],["Applebee's","dish/applebee-s"],["Arby's","dish/arby-s"],["Arnold's Bar and Grill","dish/arnold-s-bar-and-grill"],["Banana bread","dish/banana-bread"],["Banana pudding","dish/banana-pudding"],["Barbecue sauce","dish/barbecue-sauce"],["Be Our Guest Restaurant","dish/be-our-guest-restaurant"],["Beer cake","dish/beer-cake"],["Ben's Chili Bowl","dish/ben-s-chili-bowl"],["Benjy's","dish/benjy-s"],["Besaw's","dish/besaw-s"],["Better than sex cake","dish/better-than-sex-cake"],["Blackhawk (restaurant)","dish/blackhawk-restaurant"],["Blini","dish/blini"],["Blooming onion","dish/blooming-onion"],["Bobcat Bite","dish/bobcat-bite"],["Boiling Springs Tavern","dish/boiling-springs-tavern"],["Brix Tavern","dish/brix-tavern"],["Brown Betty (dessert)","dish/brown-betty-dessert"],["Brown Derby","dish/brown-derby"],["Brunswick stew","dish/brunswick-stew"],["Buffalo wing","dish/buffalo-wing"],["Buona","dish/buona"],["Busboys and Poets","dish/busboys-and-poets"],["Butter cake","dish/butter-cake"],